## OpenInference stops Anthropic calls from gaining a second trace record

Source: Arize AI — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/python-openinference-instrumentation-anthropic-v3.1.1
Published: 2026-10-29
Channel: github

OpenInference provides instrumentation that records AI application operations as traces. Its Python Anthropic integration fixes a case where the Anthropic client adds a second span to each traced call. A span is one operation record, so this change addresses duplicate representation of the same call rather than a newly observed model action.

The instrumentor stops the extra span from being added with the affected newer client behavior. The release also raises the minimum dependency on OpenInference semantic conventions, the shared definitions for trace attributes. Its short notes do not report performance measurements or describe a migration procedure. The separate runtime-compatibility releases published alongside it are not evidence of additional duplicate-span fixes.

Why it matters: Users of the Python Anthropic instrumentor can verify that one model call produces the expected trace structure after upgrading.

